repository-code: 'https://github.com/ProgrmerJack/Public-Procurement-Control-Surface'
url: 'https://github.com/ProgrmerJack/Public-Procurement-Control-Surface'
abstract: >-
  A two-part open resource for measuring competition in EU public
  procurement across two generations of reporting systems. Part A is a
  contract-level competition–carbon dataset (16.97M de-duplicated,
  carbon-mapped contracts across 33 territories, 2012–2023): an 8.18M-award
  TED portion rebuilt directly from the raw contract-award notices — which
  eliminates a 2018 ingestion artifact and recovers the bidder count across
  a schema field-rename — plus flagged non-TED sources, with a
  country×CPV×month single-bidding panel, a CPV→EXIOBASE carbon weight
  validated against Eurostat, a source-verified winner name, and Directive
  2014/24 transposition dates. Part B is a full-bid-set corpus parsed from
  EU eForms (302,555 single-award notices, 2024–2025) giving the complete
  ranked tenderer set per award.
keywords:
  - public procurement
  - Tenders Electronic Daily
  - eForms
  - single bidding
  - competition
  - EXIOBASE
  - carbon intensity
  - green public procurement
  - full bid set
  - open contracting
